ABSTRACT
The advancement of healthcare technology has made it possible to develop intelligent systems that help in the early detection of diseases. 
This mini project, "Disease Prediction from Symptoms Using Natural Language Processing (NLP),"
aims to predict diseases based on symptoms entered by users in natural language. 
It is a Multilingual Healthcare System that uses NLP techniques to process symptom descriptions and the Naive Bayes algorithm to identify the most probable disease.
Based on the predicted disease, the system provides relevant information such as recommended diet, precautions, and medicines to assist users. 
To improve accessibility and user experience, the application also supports multiple languages, allowing users to view the disease information, 
diet recommendations, precautions, and medicines in English, Assamese, Hindi, or Bengali.
The developed model achieves an accuracy of 85%,demonstrating its effectiveness in symptom-based disease prediction.
This project demonstrates the effective use of NLP and machine learning in healthcare, providing a simple, accurate, and user-friendly solution 
for symptom-based disease prediction and health guidance.
